abstract: "If technological lineages share an early cosmic start and inherit progress between environments, how much earlier than us could they have emerged without leaving visible predecessors? Under flat-space geometry and ideal detection of expanded galaxies, a saturated shared-onset model permits a lead of about 14 million years."
keywords:
  - Fermi paradox
  - hard steps
  - grabby civilisations
  - astrobiology
  - SETI
